  "preamble": "The elision of the vowel [a] is a common process of sound loss. Depending on its position in the word, it is classified as apheresis (initial), syncope (medial), or apocope (final). In Trinitario Mojeño (Arawakan, Bolivia), rhythmic syncope deleted vowels in weak metrical positions.",
